From f73a1f8466771180f4156084bc8e87edbba75cde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:34:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): human asks resolve outside Hermes via
 human_request.resolved_check [daveey]

A blocked card's human_request may carry resolved_check (+ resolved_check_every): a probe that exits 0 once
David's step happened anywhere. It runs once at filing (exit 0 refuses as ask_already_resolved, other
failures as resolved_check_broken, inline secrets as resolved_check_secret), then the dispatcher's
condition-wake sweep probes it while the card is blocked; one exit 0 comments and unblocks normally,
repeated failures comment once and stop.

Filing runs on every entry path in the card's sweep context: kanban_block / kanban_create tools, hermes
kanban block (every --ids card checked before any is blocked) / create / block --metadata-only, and the
dashboard PATCH and bulk updates. A create probes before the card exists with the target board pin and the
assignee's env but no HERMES_KANBAN_TASK (never the creator's ids); an idempotent retry runs nothing.

Synced boards: the filing gateway runs the probe (probe_host); a worker node keeps its blocked copy; a
lost probe is restored once, then commented once; permanently stopped probes take no write txn. A relayed
ask's worker notes resolved_check_alive; a silent probe host gets one home-board comment, never an unblock
or a second probe.
